# <type>: <short summary>
# Example: feat: support system preferred theme fallback
#
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature
#   fix:      A bug fix
#   refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   style:    Formatting, linting, or styling (no logic change)
#   docs:     Documentation updates (e.g. README.md, DESIGN.md)
#   test:     Adding or correcting tests
#   chore:    Build system, packages, config, or auxiliary updates
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Guidelines:
# - Subject must be 50 characters or less.
# - Capitalize the subject line.
# - Do not end the subject line with a period.
# - Use the imperative mood in the subject line (e.g. "Add" instead of "Added").
